{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, קַיָּם","hw":"קַיָּם","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">קַיָּם</span></big>  <strong>adj. enduring (</strong>cf. Nab. <span dir=\"rtl\">קים</span> (Cooke <sup>217</sup> Lzb <span dir=\"rtl\">קָיֵם</span>; SAC, privately, prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַיָּם</span>)<strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ק׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:27\" href=\"/Daniel.6.27\">Dn 6:27</a> (of God, so often 𝔗 NH, cf. Dr); fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַיָּמָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:23\" href=\"/Daniel.4.23\">4:23</a> (of kingdom).","next":"BDB Aramaic, קְטל","prev":"BDB Aramaic, קְיָם"}